  "instance_name": "armed_police_response_stereotype",
  "label": "Stereotype of police as aggressive and militarized in response to armed threats",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that police officers, especially in high-stakes situations involving armed individuals, respond with extreme force and militarized tactics. This stereotype is often used to portray law enforcement as inherently violent or overly aggressive, which can be harmful by reinforcing public perceptions of police brutality and disproportionate use of force. It implicitly references real-world controversies around police shootings and militarized policing, which are not visible in the image but are necessary to understand the meme’s intent and impact.",
